Read `.agents/skills/nomadnet-pages/SKILL.md`.

Pages are stdlib-only exec scripts and must not import `rns_resolve`. They talk
to the resolver over loopback HTTP on the private port, which is why the node
container uses host networking. Exec pages need the executable bit. Inputs
arrive as `field_*` and `var_*` environment variables.

Micron is not markdown; verify what the wire carries. MeshData head blocks
appear as literal `#` lines on the wire and are discarded at render, which is
correct. Registration through a page is attested and never replicates; the
intended flow is setup-time self-registration via `rns_resolve.nodereg`. Say
that plainly in any page copy.
